            'Ask about a person opens one thread per person inside the firm with the releasing manager, who is put on it and told (lib/threads: a firm\u2019s own thread, no other company on it)',
            'A manager reserves a person for his own project\u2019s order or, where his desk may submit, a client\u2019s job request; one hold at a time, held in the database (`ProjectHold.live` unique per person), and a second is refused naming who holds them, for what, and until when. Two weeks by default, thirty days at most; the releasing manager keeps with a date and never holds; a hold is let go by its holder or the releasing manager; a lapsed hold is read off its date',
            'The releasing manager confirms the day; nobody flagged is placed before it. The holder places: (a) on a client\u2019s job request through POST /api/submissions, where the employee goes forward as INTERNAL; or (b) a new sell line and W2 buy line on his own project\u2019s existing order, on the order\u2019s terms (`nextLineOnSameDocument`), the order line\u2019s bill rate and the pay the person is on today unless the manager types others, DRAFT with its cycles as the award writes a line, starting the day after the old line ends or on the free date, never overlapping; the old placement\u2019s end is untouched',
            'HR is told of every flag, hold, release, confirmation and move by email and in the app, and approves none of them; every step writes an attributed automation row naming who told whom',
            'The person is told at each step, never asked, by email and on their own page under \u201cYour next project\u201d; a move to another city says \u201cThis moves you from Portland to San Jose.\u201d',
            'Matching (`lib/match-pool`) reads the flag over the contract: a flagged employee free within thirty days counts, somebody kept counts from their free date, and somebody already placed onto their next project is not offered again',
            'DECIDED 2026-09-30 by the founder: a delivery manager puts the firm\u2019s own employee forward on a client\u2019s job request, as INTERNAL; somebody the firm does not employ is refused in a sentence naming the recruiting desk (src/app/api/submissions/route.ts)',
            'OPEN: skills for an integrator\u2019s employees come from a consultant profile nobody seeds for them, so the seeded Teleworld people read their seat\u2019s discipline and \u201cno skills on record\u201d, and matching cannot weigh them until somebody records skills',
            'FIXED 2026-10-01, bench tester: a hold with no date reaches the day the person is free where that is later than two weeks, and a hold asked to end sooner says it lapses first (`checkHold`); keeping somebody past their contract\u2019s end names the days with no contract under them (`keptPastContract`); a resold copy of a job request is not listed beside the one the firm was sent (`onePerJob`); a person put forward reads the client where the client belongs (`jobOnly`)',
