            'OPEN, FOUNDER \u2014 a commission run adds an agent\u2019s margin across their linked sell lines without reading each line\u2019s currency, so an agent with placements in two currencies has rupees added to dollars before anything is formatted. That is a wrong number rather than a wrong symbol, and refusing or splitting the run changes what a commission run does: what a commission on a two-currency book even is, is a product question, not an arithmetic one',
            'Pay day reaches the payroll desk a week out \u2014 the nightly scan read only the sell leg and so had never once surfaced one',
            'BUILT 2026-09-29, founder (\u201cyes to all\u201d): a nonexempt US worker is paid overtime after 40 hours a week where neither the buy line nor the sell line draws one, because the law does \u2014 in the run, on the screen, on the file and in back pay, through one door (lib/money/pay-line). A line a contract drew stands, except that a line past 40 does not hold a nonexempt US worker past the law\u2019s 40. An exempt worker keeps straight time; a worker nobody classified keeps straight time and the week over 40 says, in the existing words, that nobody has said whether they are exempt; work recorded under another country\u2019s rules, or at a site, an entity or a currency outside the US, is not held to the US 40 and the week says why. The client\u2019s bill does not move',
            'BUILT 2026-09-29, founder (\u201cyes to all\u201d): pay is the hours the employer accepted, never the hours filed, and where fewer are accepted the cut comes off ordinary hours first, from the latest day backward, so the worker keeps their overtime \u2014 the opposite of the bill\u2019s cut, on purpose. One allocation for the run, the screen, the file and back pay (lib/money/pay-hours): 45 worked and 42 accepted on a 40-hour line pays 37 ordinary and 5 overtime, and 41 accepted pays 36 and 5',
            'BUILT 2026-09-29, founder: an acceptance at or under the line is the hours worked. Where the employer accepts 40 hours or fewer of a longer week \u2014 the line in force, the contract\u2019s own or the law\u2019s 40 \u2014 those hours are paid at straight time: 38 of 45 pays 38, 40 of 45 pays 40. The line is judged on hours worked, never on paid leave. The week says so on the payroll screen, in the run and as a note on the payroll file (\u201c38 of 45 hours accepted; paid at straight time because the accepted week is not over 40.\u201d); the file pays it rather than leaving it off, and back pay tops it up at straight time with no premium. sheetPay (lib/money/sheet-overtime) is the one call a worker\u2019s page makes for a cut week. Replaces the hold the first version carried',
            'Every hour is paid at the rate in force on the day it was worked, and overtime in a week paid at two rates is priced on the US regular rate (29 CFR \u00a7778.115) by default',
            'The paying firm may choose another overtime method on the pay line \u2014 the rate on the day, or the higher rate \u2014 recorded with who chose it, when and why; anything but the default needs a reason, and only a desk that reads what people cost may change it. Founder, 2026-09-29',
            'Whatever is chosen, a nonexempt US worker is never paid less than the regular-rate premium, and the week says when the law\u2019s figure was paid instead',
            'FIXED 2026-09-29 by etyme-money: the payroll file (src/app/api/payroll/export/route.ts) reads the overtime-method columns on the buy line, so it pays the method the run pays rather than the default',
            'BUILT 2026-09-30 by etyme-money, founder-approved for the seeded world only: a demo employer pays monthly \u2014 worked out at month-end + 4 and paid at month-end + 9, measured as the smallest pair where no pay day comes before its hours and the calculation is always two days ahead of pay after a weekend or holiday moves both back. writeCyclesFor takes it as an override (DEMO_MONTHLY_PAY in lib/contract-cycles) that moves only the two pay kinds and only on a payroll line; no pack ships it and only lib/seed-* and lib/demo-* may pass it. DONE 2026-09-30 by the architect: every seeded and demo payroll line passes it (lib/seed-doors, seed-world, seed-programmes, seed-rate-change, seed-sector-suppliers, demo-placement, demo-seed-consultant), and Karthik Menon\u2019s placement is three whole months with a pay day for each',
            'BUILT 2026-09-30 by etyme-money, founder (\u201cgo with your recommendations, but keep settings user configurable\u201d): a week accepted over the line is cut by the pay line\u2019s own rule, read once by cutOvertimeFor. The default pays overtime only on the accepted hours above the line \u2014 41 of 45 pays 40 + 1, 42 pays 40 + 2 \u2014 and a firm that keeps the week\u2019s overtime, named and reasoned, is paid ordinary-first \u2014 41 pays 36 + 5. The rule is a required argument in lib/money/pay-hours, so the run, its screen, the payroll file, back pay and the worker\u2019s page cannot pay the default to a worker whose employer chose otherwise. At or under the line is straight time either way; the bill is not touched',
