            'BUILT 2026-09-30, founder (\u201cgo with your recommendations, but keep settings user configurable\u201d): each pay line carries how overtime is paid when fewer hours are accepted than were worked \u2014 \u201cOnly accepted hours over 40 (default, what the law requires)\u201d or \u201cKeep the week\u2019s overtime (ordinary hours cut first)\u201d \u2014 chosen on the placement\u2019s pay line by the firm that pays, from a desk that reads what people cost; keeping the week\u2019s overtime needs a reason, and the choice is recorded with who, when and why (PATCH /api/placements/:id/cut-overtime). Payroll reads it through one call, cutOvertimeFor in lib/cut-overtime-choice',
